    "perplexity": {
      "description": "“Complete B Sides: 1988–97 (Remastered)” by Pixies is an expanded and remastered reissue of the 2001 compilation Complete B-Sides, originally released during the band’s decade-long hiatus. This 2026 edition, part of Pixies’ 40th anniversary celebrations, gathers all 19 non-album B-sides from their legendary 1988–1991 4AD-era singles—including iconic tracks like “Wave of Mutilation (UK Surf)”, “Into The White” (sung by Kim Deal), and “Bailey’s Walk”—and extends the collection to include material up to 1997. The entire album has been meticulously remastered from the original analogue tapes by Kevin Vanbergen, restoring the raw, groundbreaking energy that defined the indie-rock pioneers’ classic run.\n\nBeyond the original tracklist, this remaster adds six bonus live tracks culled from later Pixies single releases, such as the 1997 re-release of “Debaser”, offering a dynamic companion to the band’s recent Live at the BBC reissue. The compilation is now available on vinyl for the first time in its history—as a 2LP set on black or clear vinyl—as well as a 2CD edition, marking a significant milestone for collectors. With striking new artwork by designer Chris Bigg, featuring previously shelved photos from Simon Larbalestier’s archive, the release not only preserves the band’s timeless “other” tracks but also enhances their legacy with fresh sonic clarity and visual depth.",
